{"slug":"science","main":"<div data-page-top-spacer=\"condensed\" class=\"bg-default\"><section class=\"ZSMdoa_root\" data-theme=\"ivory\"><div class=\"Bo9kyq_container\" data-component=\"CSSGrid.Container\"><h1 class=\"LOCOdG_text\" style=\"visibility: visible; translate: none; rotate: none; scale: none; transform: translate(0px, 0px); opacity: 1;\"><span class=\"LOCOdG_lead\"><button type=\"button\" data-lead-control=\"true\" class=\"v9lDbq_button\">The Science effort<span class=\"v9lDbq_mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"_6xvBMG_mark v9lDbq_markImage\" style=\"mask-image: url(&quot;/sites/anthropic/sanity/888b2270623ed548bb2b6514024d49757127cf47-1152x1088.webp&quot;); mask-size: 1800% 1700%; mask-position: 88.2353% 37.5%;\"></span></span></button></span> <span class=\"LOCOdG_statement\">at Anthropic focuses on how AI can increase the pace of scientific progress. We work to improve our models’ core scientific capabilities and enable practitioners to use them to make scientific and technological advancements. We also aim to increase the pace of AI-driven science through partnerships, grants, and internal research in areas such as drug development and molecular biology.</span></h1></div></section><section class=\"ZSMdoa_root\" data-theme=\"ivory\"><div class=\"Bo9kyq_container\" data-component=\"CSSGrid.Container\"><div class=\"Bo9kyq_standard Bo9kyq_flow-row NEQLZG_grid\" data-component=\"CSSGrid.Standard\"><div class=\"Bo9kyq_m-full Bo9kyq_t-span-5 Bo9kyq_d-span-4 NEQLZG_metadata\" data-component=\"CSSGrid.Item\"><div style=\"visibility: visible; translate: none; rotate: none; scale: none; transform: translate(0px, 0px); opacity: 1;\"><dl class=\"kpV0Dq_articleMeta\"><div class=\"kpV0Dq_articleMetaItem\"><dt>AI for Science</dt><dd><a href=\"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11199177-anthropic-s-ai-for-science-program\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"kpV0Dq_articleMetaItemLink\"><span>Visit</span><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 14 14\" fill=\"currentColor\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"flex-shrink:0\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M11.4999 2.00017C11.776 2.00017 11.9999 2.22403 11.9999 2.50017V9.5002C11.9998 9.7762 11.7759 10.0002 11.4999 10.0002C11.2239 10.0001 11 9.7762 10.9999 9.5002V3.7072L2.85338 11.8537C2.6581 12.0488 2.34155 12.0489 2.14635 11.8537C1.95116 11.6585 1.95127 11.3419 2.14635 11.1467L10.2928 3.00017H4.49986C4.22387 3.00006 3.99995 2.77617 3.99986 2.50017C3.99986 2.22409 4.22381 2.00028 4.49986 2.00017H11.4999Z\"></path></svg></a></dd></div><div class=\"kpV0Dq_articleMetaItem\"><dt>Claude Science</dt><dd><a href=\"https://claude.com/product/claude-science\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"kpV0Dq_articleMetaItemLink\"><span>Learn more</span><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 14 14\" fill=\"currentColor\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"flex-shrink:0\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M11.4999 2.00017C11.776 2.00017 11.9999 2.22403 11.9999 2.50017V9.5002C11.9998 9.7762 11.7759 10.0002 11.4999 10.0002C11.2239 10.0001 11 9.7762 10.9999 9.5002V3.7072L2.85338 11.8537C2.6581 12.0488 2.34155 12.0489 2.14635 11.8537C1.95116 11.6585 1.95127 11.3419 2.14635 11.1467L10.2928 3.00017H4.49986C4.22387 3.00006 3.99995 2.77617 3.99986 2.50017C3.99986 2.22409 4.22381 2.00028 4.49986 2.00017H11.4999Z\"></path></svg></a></dd></div></dl></div></div><div class=\"Bo9kyq_m-full Bo9kyq_t-span-7 Bo9kyq_t-start-6 Bo9kyq_d-span-8 Bo9kyq_d-start-5 NEQLZG_textCell\" data-component=\"CSSGrid.Item\"><div class=\"NEQLZG_texts\"><div class=\"NEQLZG_text js-stagger-item\" style=\"visibility: visible; translate: none; rotate: none; scale: none; transform: translate(0px, 0px); opacity: 0;\" data-animated=\"true\"><h3 class=\"tOQyXa_headline-5 NEQLZG_heading\" data-component=\"Headline\">Research</h3><p class=\"tOQyXa_body-3\" data-component=\"Body\">The scientific and discovery process consists of feedback loops: designing and conducting an experiment, interpreting the results, revising the question, and beginning again. We’re working to tighten these loops by developing tools that make researchers more efficient or help them develop entirely new approaches, and by building training environments and evaluations that help us improve Claude’s performance on scientific tasks.</p></div><div class=\"NEQLZG_text js-stagger-item\" style=\"visibility: visible; translate: none; rotate: none; scale: none; transform: translate(0px, 0px); opacity: 0;\" data-animated=\"true\"><h3 class=\"tOQyXa_headline-5 NEQLZG_heading\" data-component=\"Headline\">AI for Science</h3><p class=\"tOQyXa_body-3\" data-component=\"Body\">We work with universities, research institutes, biotech companies, and academic medical centers—through direct API access, co-developed custom agents, applied AI technical support, and more—to get Claude into the hands of scientists. This allows us to incorporate feedback based on real-world evaluation and applied research across domains, demonstrating the tangible impacts AI is having on science.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class=\"ZSMdoa_root\" data-theme=\"ivory\"><div class=\"_5NNTzG_inset-frame\"><div class=\"_5NNTzG_hero-carousel _5NNTzG_unthemed _5NNTzG_inset\" style=\"visibility: visible; translate: none; rotate: none; scale: none; transform: translate(0px, 0px); opacity: 0;\"><div class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-wrapper\"><div class=\"_5NNTzG_embla-viewport\"><ul class=\"_5NNTzG_embla-container\" style=\"transform: translate3d(0px, 0px, 0px);\"><li class=\"_5NNTzG_embla-slide\" style=\"transform: translate3d(0px, 0px, 0px);\"><a class=\"_5NNTzG_slide-link\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" href=\"/research/investigating-vault-particles-with-claude\"><img alt=\"Collage illustration pairing vintage measuring scales over a black-and-white photograph with a green print of a ribbed, vaulted cathedral ceiling.\" loading=\"eager\" width=\"1407\" height=\"793\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" style=\"color:transparent\" sizes=\"100vw\" src=\"/sites/anthropic/pages-assets/a55e95ad6b28a73846ad.jpg\"></a></li><li class=\"_5NNTzG_embla-slide\"><a class=\"_5NNTzG_slide-link\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" href=\"/research/claude-scorpion-toxin-binder-design\"><img alt=\"How Claude designed protein binders against scorpion neurotoxins\" loading=\"eager\" width=\"1407\" height=\"793\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" style=\"color:transparent\" sizes=\"100vw\" src=\"/sites/anthropic/pages-assets/a0e12fb1a8f68ac9a97b.webp\"></a></li><li class=\"_5NNTzG_embla-slide\"><a class=\"_5NNTzG_slide-link\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" href=\"/research/claude-shaped-science\"><img alt=\"Claude-shaped science\" loading=\"eager\" width=\"1407\" height=\"793\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" style=\"color:transparent\" sizes=\"100vw\" src=\"/sites/anthropic/pages-assets/653852642b00759afc4c.webp\"></a></li><li class=\"_5NNTzG_embla-slide\"><a class=\"_5NNTzG_slide-link\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" href=\"/research/formalizing-fermats-last-theorem\"><img alt=\"Formalizing Fermat's Last Theorem\" loading=\"eager\" width=\"1407\" height=\"793\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" style=\"color:transparent\" sizes=\"100vw\" src=\"/sites/anthropic/pages-assets/ceb59fcf468db08db21e.webp\"></a></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info\"><div class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-slides\"><div class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-body\"><header class=\"nUeDbq_header _5NNTzG_carousel-info-meta\"><div class=\"nUeDbq_headerButton\"><button aria-label=\"Related to Investigating vault particles with Claude\" class=\"hN4zBq_tiny-more-button hN4zBq_state-closed\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-base-ui-click-trigger=\"\" id=\"base-ui-_R_f95l9qnpfcnpfkq6btb_\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"hN4zBq_icon\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\"><use href=\"#tiny-more-button-close\"></use></svg><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"hN4zBq_icon hN4zBq_icon-visible\" width=\"12\" height=\"2\"><use href=\"#tiny-more-button-more\"></use></svg></button></div><p><a class=\"wN10Da_link\" href=\"/science\">Science</a></p><time class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-date\">Nov 4, 2026</time></header><a class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-link\" href=\"/research/investigating-vault-particles-with-claude\"><h2 class=\"tOQyXa_headline-5 _5NNTzG_carousel-info-title\" data-component=\"Headline\">Investigating vault particles with Claude</h2></a><p class=\"tOQyXa_body-4 _5NNTzG_carousel-info-description\" data-component=\"Body\">We’re sharing another finding from Anthropic’s biology research lab: the first 3D structure of a vault particle found in prokaryotic cells. Here, we describe how Claude helped at each step of this research.</p></div><div class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-body\" data-inactive=\"true\" aria-hidden=\"true\" inert=\"\"><header class=\"nUeDbq_header _5NNTzG_carousel-info-meta\"><div class=\"nUeDbq_headerButton\"><button aria-label=\"Related to How Claude designed protein binders against scorpion neurotoxins\" class=\"hN4zBq_tiny-more-button hN4zBq_state-closed\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-base-ui-click-trigger=\"\" id=\"base-ui-_R_f99l9qnpfcnpfkq6btb_\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"hN4zBq_icon\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\"><use href=\"#tiny-more-button-close\"></use></svg><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"hN4zBq_icon hN4zBq_icon-visible\" width=\"12\" height=\"2\"><use href=\"#tiny-more-button-more\"></use></svg></button></div><p><a class=\"wN10Da_link\" href=\"/science\">Science</a></p><time class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-date\">Oct 20, 2026</time></header><a class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-link\" href=\"/research/claude-scorpion-toxin-binder-design\"><h2 class=\"tOQyXa_headline-5 _5NNTzG_carousel-info-title\" data-component=\"Headline\">How Claude designed protein binders against scorpion neurotoxins</h2></a><p class=\"tOQyXa_body-4 _5NNTzG_carousel-info-description\" data-component=\"Body\">We asked an internal research Claude model to design minibinders (small proteins that attach tightly to a target) against scorpion neurotoxins.</p></div><div class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-body\" data-inactive=\"true\" aria-hidden=\"true\" inert=\"\"><header class=\"nUeDbq_header _5NNTzG_carousel-info-meta\"><div class=\"nUeDbq_headerButton\"><button aria-label=\"Related to Claude-shaped science\" class=\"hN4zBq_tiny-more-button hN4zBq_state-closed\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-base-ui-click-trigger=\"\" id=\"base-ui-_R_f9dl9qnpfcnpfkq6btb_\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"hN4zBq_icon\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\"><use href=\"#tiny-more-button-close\"></use></svg><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"hN4zBq_icon hN4zBq_icon-visible\" width=\"12\" height=\"2\"><use href=\"#tiny-more-button-more\"></use></svg></button></div><p><a class=\"wN10Da_link\" href=\"/science\">Science</a></p><time class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-date\">Oct 1, 2026</time></header><a class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-link\" href=\"/research/claude-shaped-science\"><h2 class=\"tOQyXa_headline-5 _5NNTzG_carousel-info-title\" data-component=\"Headline\">Claude-shaped science</h2></a><p class=\"tOQyXa_body-4 _5NNTzG_carousel-info-description\" data-component=\"Body\">Guest author Prof. Matthew Schwartz describes what happened when he stopped fighting Claude and allowed Claude to find “Claude-shaped” problems: ones best suited to the capabilities of the current generation of LLM tools. This led him to build BootLoops, a toolkit for exact calculations in quantitative science, which he has been applying across scientific fields alongside experts.</p><a href=\"/research/claude-shaped-science\" class=\"f9ZZrG_button f9ZZrG_corner-small f9ZZrG_variant-secondary f9ZZrG_size-small f9ZZrG_icon-format-trailing _5NNTzG_carousel-info-cta\">Read more<span class=\"f9ZZrG_icon\"><svg class=\"lqbdHG_icon\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 21 21\"><path d=\"M4.14585 9.87492L14.4584 9.87492L9.60419 5.04158L10.5 4.14575L16.8542 10.4999L10.5 16.8541L9.60419 15.9583L14.4584 11.1249L4.14585 11.1249L4.14585 9.87492Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></svg></span></a></div><div class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-body\" data-inactive=\"true\" aria-hidden=\"true\" inert=\"\"><header class=\"nUeDbq_header _5NNTzG_carousel-info-meta\"><div class=\"nUeDbq_headerButton\"><button aria-label=\"Related to Formalizing Fermat's Last Theorem \" class=\"hN4zBq_tiny-more-button hN4zBq_state-closed\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-base-ui-click-trigger=\"\" id=\"base-ui-_R_f9hl9qnpfcnpfkq6btb_\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"hN4zBq_icon\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\"><use href=\"#tiny-more-button-close\"></use></svg><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"hN4zBq_icon hN4zBq_icon-visible\" width=\"12\" height=\"2\"><use href=\"#tiny-more-button-more\"></use></svg></button></div><p><a class=\"wN10Da_link\" href=\"/science\">Science</a></p><time class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-date\">Sep 4, 2026</time></header><a class=\"_5NNTzG_carousel-info-link\" href=\"/research/formalizing-fermats-last-theorem\"><h2 class=\"tOQyXa_headline-5 _5NNTzG_carousel-info-title\" data-component=\"Headline\">Formalizing Fermat's Last Theorem </h2></a><p class=\"tOQyXa_body-4 _5NNTzG_carousel-info-description\" data-component=\"Body\">We are sharing the first complete computer-checked proof of Fermat’s Last Theorem. Claude worked largely autonomously over 11 days to write the proof in the Lean programming language.</p><a href=\"/research/formalizing-fermats-last-theorem\" class=\"f9ZZrG_button f9ZZrG_corner-small f9ZZrG_variant-secondary f9ZZrG_size-small f9ZZrG_icon-format-trailing _5NNTzG_carousel-info-cta\">Read more<span class=\"f9ZZrG_icon\"><svg class=\"lqbdHG_icon\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 21 21\"><path d=\"M4.14585 9.8